=== PARITY ===
Ported web/src/api/hooks/useAnnotations.ts (2 reads + 3 mutations = 5 hooks) ->
AnnotationRepository (S7) + HttpAnnotationRepository + AnnotationsStore (S8). UI-free; SI preserved.

Reads (2):
 1. useChartAnnotations(params)        -> AnnotationsStore.chartAnnotations(params) : StateFlow<Resource<List<ChartAnnotationRow>>>
        GET /annotations/?vehicle_id=&scope=&from=&to=   (annotationQuery mirrors web buildQuery:
        vehicle_id sent whenever present via !=null; scope/from/to only when non-blank via the JS truthy guard).
        Cache-then-network (ADR-013); typed List<ChartAnnotationRow> cached under annotationCacheKey,
        which reproduces the web annotationKeys.list tuple ['annotations', vehicleId??'all', scope??'all', from??'', to??''].
        TTL = CacheDomain.Annotations 5.minutes == web STALE_TIMES.SLOW (5*60_000).
 2. useChartAnnotationsAsData(params)  -> AnnotationsStore.chartAnnotationsAsData(params) : StateFlow<Resource<List<DataAnnotation>>>
        The SAME shared upstream re-projected through toDataAnnotation (one fetch backs both views, exactly
        like the web wrapper reusing the same TanStack query key -- asserted in AnnotationsStoreTest).
        Web { annotations, isLoading } maps onto Resource: annotations = data/cached list, isLoading = (it is Resource.Loading).

Mutations (3) -- each mirrors web invalidateAndBroadcast(qc, { queryKey: annotationKeys.all }):
 3. useCreateAnnotation -> store.createAnnotation(input) : Result<ChartAnnotationRow>
        POST /annotations/   body { occurred_at, category, title (+ vehicle_id/description/scope/color only when present,
        mirroring JSON.stringify dropping undefined keys) }  -> repo evicts the WHOLE CacheDomain.Annotations partition (clear)
        + store.refreshAll() re-collects every observed feed.
 4. useUpdateAnnotation -> store.updateAnnotation(input) : Result<ChartAnnotationRow>
        PATCH /annotations/{id}   body = only the changed fields; clear_description/clear_color sent only when set
        (explicit erasers) -> clear() + refreshAll().
 5. useDeleteAnnotation -> store.deleteAnnotation(id) : Result<Unit>
        DELETE /annotations/{id}   (server 204 No Content read as raw text and discarded) -> clear() + refreshAll().

Invalidate-all semantics: the web hooks invalidate annotationKeys.all (the whole 'annotations' tree) because a write can
affect any (vehicle, scope, window) list -- a fleet-wide row (vehicle_id NULL) appears on every vehicle. The data layer
evicts the ENTIRE partition; the store bumps every observed feed's trigger (the as-data feeds re-derive automatically
because they observe the raw feeds). A FAILED mutation leaves the cache untouched (asserted: mutationFailureDoesNotInvalidate).
A feed nobody observes is a no-op refresh (asserted: refreshAllIsNoOpWhenNothingIsObserved).

Derivations golden-locked for KMP+C# parity (AnnotationsGoldenTest, ADR-004; language-neutral JSON in / fixed out):
  - toDataAnnotation   : id stringified, label=title, context = scope[0] ?? '', null-preserving description/vehicleId
                         (cases: full_row, fleet_wide_null_vehicle, scopeless_row, multi_scope_takes_first, null_description).
  - annotationQuery    : vehicle_id always-when-present; blank scope/from/to dropped
                         (cases: empty, vehicle_only, all_params, blank_optionals_dropped, scope_only).
  - annotationCacheKey : web annotationKeys.list null-coalescing; the subtle edge where an empty scope stays '' in the KEY
                         even though it is dropped from the QUERY (case: empty_scope_stays_empty).

SI: annotation fields are ids / timestamps / titles / hex colours -- not unit-bearing -- so they round-trip verbatim as
typed ChartAnnotationRow JSON; no conversion at this layer (display formatting is the S5 render boundary's job).

Endpoints verified against internal/api/router.go (r.Route("/annotations"): Get "/", Post "/", Patch "/{id}", Delete "/{id}")
and the web wire shape in web/src/types/annotations.ts (ChartAnnotationRow / DataAnnotation / toDataAnnotation).

